{"text": "Pemberton Ashby Solicitors LLP\n\nATTENDANCE NOTE (privileged)\n\nField\tDetail\n\nClient\tMrs Folasade Adeyemi-Clarke\n\nMatter\tADE0417/0002\n\nFee earner\tRJP\n\nDate\t3 February 2026\n\nAttendance\tIn person, 55 minutes\n\nOpponent\tNorthgate Logistics (UK) Ltd\n\nIdentity and contact (AML check completed)\n\nItem\tValue\n\nKnown as\tSade\n\nDate of birth\t14 March 1979\n\nNI number\tJK 47 21 09 C\n\nPassport\t533184726\n\nDriving licence\tADEYE753149FA9KL\n\nAddress\t27 Cardigan Lane\n\nArea\tHeadingley, Leeds\n\nPostcode\tLS6 3BJ\n\nMobile\t07700 900143\n\nEmail\tsade.ac@postbox.example\n\nBackground\n\nMrs Adeyemi-Clarke worked for Northgate as a transport planner at its Stourton depot from 1 September 2017 until she was dismissed on 19 December 2025. Her salary was £31,200 a year. She was diagnosed with relapsing-remitting multiple sclerosis in 2023 and told her line manager, Gareth Whitcombe, at the time. Occupational health recommended a later start and two home-working days; these were in place until Mr Whitcombe withdrew them in September \"for operational reasons\".\n\nShe raised a grievance on 06/10/2025. It was heard by the depot manager, Imran Qureshi, and rejected. She was then put on a performance plan and dismissed for capability eleven weeks later. She is a union member and her branch rep attended both meetings; Sade says the rep's notes record Whitcombe saying \"we can't carry people\". She also mentioned, hesitantly, that she had asked to swap her Friday late shift so she could attend Jumu'ah prayers and was refused; I do not think that is a separate claim, but it is relevant background.\n\nShe had two relapses in the autumn and is currently on ocrelizumab infusions every six months. She has been signed off with anxiety since January. Her husband, Desmond, is the only earner at present.\n\nAdvice given\n\n- Claims: unfair dismissal (Employment Rights Act 1996), failure to make reasonable adjustments (section 20, Equality Act 2010) and discrimination arising from disability.\n\n- Time limit: ACAS early conciliation must start by 18 March 2026. Certificate ref will be needed for the ET1.\n\n- Prospects: reasonable to good on adjustments; I put overall prospects at about 60%.\n\n- Likely value: basic award about £5,400; compensatory award and injury to feelings together in the range £18,000 to £27,000.\n\nFunding\n\nShe has legal expenses cover with her home insurance through Aire Valley Legal Protection plc, policy HH/7741093/LP. I will ask Aire Valley to confirm cover and my appointment. Until then we act on a fixed fee of £450 plus VAT for the ACAS stage, which she paid today by debit card ending 9130.\n\nAny refund or damages to be paid to her joint account at Yorkshire Dales Building Society: sort code 40-47-21, account 41906532, IBAN GB39 NWBK 3875 8627 1563 32.\n\nActions\n\n- RJP to send client care letter and notify ACAS this week.\n\n- Niamh Gallagher (trainee) to request the personnel file and occupational health reports by subject access request.\n\n- Client to send payslips, the dismissal letter and her diary of the autumn meetings.\n\n- Diary: review 17/02/2026.\n\nTime recorded: 9 units. Rupert Pemberton, Partner. Direct line 0113 496 0127.", "kind": "Web page", "detail": "500 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Mrs Folasade Adeyemi-Clarke", "Sade", "Gareth Whitcombe", "Imran Qureshi", "Desmond", "Niamh Gallagher"], "companies": ["Northgate Logistics (UK) Ltd", "ACAS", "Aire Valley Legal Protection plc", "Yorkshire Dales Building Society"]}, "topics": {"places": [], "health": [], "sensitive": [], "names": []}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 2.2999999970197678, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing"